{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And He drove out the man.</b> This is not written to say that HaShem drove him out, for it was already stated, 'and He sent him out.' Rather, this is its meaning: when He drove him out, He stationed the cherubim." "<b>The cherubim.</b> Forms that terrify those who see them, and in their hands <b>the flame of the sword that turns</b> — which has a flame on both its sides."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:51.109725518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}